WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.269
Hi, I'm Macaron!

00:00:02.269 --> 00:00:04.880
Jev picks from a list but can't write.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.797
Five repositories, read side by side, each built the same four parts.

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:11.851
A decision model only picks.

00:00:11.851 --> 00:00:16.251
So every harness builds an enumerator, a question format, a confidence gate,

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:18.085
and a composer for strings.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:23.505
The environment is observed, and its finite action space is compiled into

00:00:23.505 --> 00:00:26.870
typed questions: pick one, yes or no, or a score.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.036
Every question for the step rides one request.

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:33.126
One model call per step, and no generated actions.

00:00:33.546 --> 00:00:37.555
A gate checks the weakest judgment the action needs against a threshold

00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:38.891
set by its risk.

00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:42.566
Above it, the action runs, and the trace keeps every probability.

00:00:42.986 --> 00:00:46.019
Below it, nothing runs, and the step is refused.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:49.727
Three refusals end the run, with a handoff: its questions, answers

00:00:49.727 --> 00:00:51.075
and the threshold missed.

00:00:51.495 --> 00:00:55.162
The price of one call: the compiler refuses any parameter that

00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:56.496
would need free text.

00:00:56.496 --> 00:01:00.163
Strings are supplied by the operator, by name, before the run.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.299
Below the threshold, System One Harness refuses.

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:06.263
The search tool drops the result.

00:01:07.428 --> 00:01:10.069
The browser agent escalates to a language model.

00:01:10.489 --> 00:01:12.782
And the diffusion server takes three more reads.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:16.334
One probe reads a game from pixels.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.486
Always answering the commonest key scores point nine seven.

00:01:19.486 --> 00:01:22.637
No encoding beats it; the best scores point five.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:27.022
So the decision model is a policy you can swap in.

00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:30.572
The engineering is everything around it, and the enumerator most of all.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.690
To recap: four parts around a model that only picks, one call

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.639
per step, and an enumerator that makes or breaks it.

00:01:39.059 --> 00:01:41.195
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:41.805
I'm Macaron.

00:01:41.805 --> 00:01:42.110
Bye!
